/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  Case-local PARTIAL overlay of the standard acetone record: the HANSEN
  TRIPLE, which no catalogue record carries (DEV.md 4c C128).
  `overlayOf acetone;` declares this a DELTA -- the reader deep-merges it over
  data/standards/components/acetone.dat, so MW, Vliq, the vapour pressure and
  everything else keep coming from the standard.

  SOURCE, per value: Hansen, C. M., The Three Dimensional Solubility Parameter and Solvent Diffusion Coefficient: Their Importance in Surface Coating Formulation, doctoral dissertation, Danish Technical Press, Copenhagen (1967), Table 2.1 (pages 18-19), row 29
  "Acetone", the REVISED placements: delta_d = 7.58, delta_p = 5.1,
  delta_h = 3.4 (cal/cm3)^0.5.  Converted to Pa^0.5 by sqrt(4.184e6) =
  2045.4828; the thesis's own digits are the ones in the comments.
  Tref: the thesis prints no temperature beside Table 2.1; its placements
  were checked against solubility tests at room temperature, and 25 C is the
  reference every later compilation of these values states.  Adopted as
  298.15 K, flagged interim.  reviewStatus interim: transcribed from the
  page image (not the OCR text, whose columns are scrambled) and not yet
  read back by a second person.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
overlayOf acetone;

hansen
{
    dD    15504.8;        // Pa^0.5   = 7.58 (cal/cm3)^0.5, thesis Table 2.1 row 29
    dP    10432.0;        // Pa^0.5   = 5.1
    dH    6954.6;        // Pa^0.5   = 3.4
    Tref  298.15 K;       // adopted (see the header); no correction exists in the engine
}

provenance
{
    hansen
    {
        origin        literature;
        method        "Hansen 1967 thesis, Table 2.1 row 29 (Acetone), revised placements; (cal/cm3)^0.5 x 2045.4828 -> Pa^0.5";
        reviewStatus  interim;
        notes         "transcribed from the page image 2026-10-21; Tref 298.15 K adopted, the thesis states no temperature beside the table";
    }
}
